Teserra is a C++20 game engine in development: https://github.com/fyernald/teserra

$description

Running it
----------
1. Unzip this folder anywhere (for example, your Desktop).
2. Double-click $executable.
3. Press Escape or close the window to quit.

Windows may show a "Windows protected your PC" (SmartScreen) message, because the program is new and not
code-signed. Choose "More info", then "Run anyway". The program does not install anything and only writes
teserra.log into this folder.

Requirements: 64-bit Windows 10 or 11 and a graphics driver with OpenGL 4.5 (most GPUs since 2014 with
current drivers). The Visual C++ runtime it needs is included.

Feedback
--------
Please tell us whether it worked, even if it did:
$feedback_url

Useful to include: what you saw, your Windows version, your GPU and driver version, and the teserra.log file
from this folder (it lists the GPU and OpenGL version and any error).

